            <div xml:id="d421">

                <pb facs="0684" n="656" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v21/pg656"/>

                <head>421. Memorandum From Secretary of State Rusk to President Kennedy<anchor n="0" xml:id="d421-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1963-11-06">November 6,
                        1963</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Security Council Meeting on South Africa</item>
                </list>
                <p>Enclosed is a paper<anchor n="1" xml:id="d421-f2"/> which describes the approach
                    we plan to take in the forthcoming Security Council meeting on the problem of
                    apartheid in South Africa. This policy has been developed in close consultation
                    with Ambassador Stevenson.</p>
                <p>We propose to continue opposing mandatory sanctions and to indicate clearly the
                    limits of UN measures which we think appropriate
                    to deal with the problem. At the same time, in order to show our continuing
                    concern about apartheid and to help deflect support from a more radical
                    resolution, we would be prepared to interpret our existing policy on arms
                    restrictions to include an embargo on materials used primarily in the production
                    of arms and ammunition. The Norwegians have developed such a proposition;
                    Governor Stevenson will be working with
                    them and other Council members to obtain a resolution satisfactory to us. In
                    addition, we would be prepared to accept a suitable version of an expert
                    committee to study the South African problem.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Dean
                            Rusk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
